1. Axis-aligned (sides parallel to matrix edges)
2. Diagonal (sides parallel to matrix diagonals - diamond shape)

Key constraints:
- Must be a frame (border) with linewidth 1
- Must contain at least one 1
- Cannot touch (side or corner) any foreign 1
- Must be at least 2x2
- All sides must be equal

A "solid square frame" means border cells are 1, interior can be 0 or 1, but NO cell on the interior can be adjacent to any exterior 1.

